# NOTICE

## What the licence covers

`LICENSE` is an MIT grant over **this project's own work**: the platform layer
under `platform/`, the build and packaging scripts, the tests, the tooling under
`tools/`, and the documentation under `docs/`. Those files carry no licence
header of their own, so this is where their terms are stated.

## What it does not cover

**The game code is not covered, and cannot be.** `src/` and `include/` are a
recompilation of *Metroid Prime* (`GM8E01`, USA v1.00) from the retail
executable. That material is Nintendo's, no permission to redistribute it is
asserted here, and the MIT grant above deliberately stops at the repository
root's own code rather than sweeping those directories in. Anyone who obtained
this repository obtained a working copy; that is a separate question from what
may be redistributed, and it is one only the copyright holder can answer.

**The console SDK and runtime are not covered either.** `extern/sdk/` holds the
decompiled Dolphin (GameCube) SDK (`extern/sdk/dolphin/`, which still carries
Nintendo's build strings), the Metrowerks C library headers (`extern/sdk/libc/`)
and the CodeWarrior runtime (`extern/sdk/runtime/`). Like `src/` and
`include/`, they come from the retail executable and its toolchain, belong to
their owners, and are outside the MIT grant. The same goes for the per-revision
symbol and split data under `config/`, which describes that executable.

**No game assets may be packaged with a build.** Not the disc image, not
extracted PAK/STRG data, not textures from the retail game. The build takes the
disc image as a runtime argument and nothing else, and `tools/make_appimage.sh`
says so in its own help text. The only images the port ships are its own
controller-button glyphs, regenerated by `tools/make_prompt_glyphs.py` from
CC0 sources.

